OL,3,GNEWSAThe man who chooses to sleep with
OL,4,Abedbugs
OL,5,
OL,6,FA scientist has chosen to sleep with
OL,7,Fbedbugs for the past five years - and
OL,8,Fsays the bites "don't bother him at
OL,9,Fall".
OL,11,FEntomologist Dr Richard Naylor breeds
OL,12,Fthousands of bedbugs to test pest
OL,13,Fcontrol products from all over the
OL,14,Fworld and allows himself to be the test
OL,15,Fsubject.
OL,17,FOn a "feeding day", which happens
OL,18,Faround twice a week, he straps some of
OL,19,Fhis 50-60,000 bugs to his arm and gets
OL,20,Fon with his work.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,343,340,200,160,0,100
